my dad risked everything to be with his  family and this is that story growing up  in some Paulo Brazil  my dad had always dreamt of traveling  the world when he was in his early 20s  he convinced two buddies of his from  church the Church of Jesus Christ of  latter-day saints  better known as the Mormon Church to go  on this adventure with him packing  everything they need in their backpacks  they set off with a little bit of cash  they had they'd rely on the generosity  of random folks to get to the next town  in the next city and the next state they  traveled through Chile Peru Colombia and  Ecuador after gradually making their way  northward through South America these  three amigos or today's amigos settled  for a little while in Panama after a  year there my dad was ready to move on  and his two friends decided to stay  behind in Panama so my dad continued  northward through Central America on his  own he eventually made his way to  Tijuana the city in northern Mexico just  across the border from San Diego oddly  enough he ran into some Mormon  missionaries who told them about how  every morning they walk up the beach  along the Pacific Ocean wave at the  Border Patrol agent and stroll right  into the u.s. they arranged for an  American citizen to take his belongings  for him so he wouldn't with suspicious  and so he strolled right into America  easy right  eventually he'd find his way to Los  Angeles and my daddy gets a job working  in a factory working among Mexican  Americans his Spanish was perfect but he  wasn't learning any English he decided  he needed to immerse himself to find a  community and to teach himself English  the best place to do that was obviously  Salt Lake City Utah aka  the Mormon Holy Land cut to Salt Lake  City he has a job delivering pizza he's  taking English classes which is where he  later meets my mom which is adorable I  know at 24 he enlisted at the local high  school for troubled teens despite having  just barely learned English he graduated  at the top of his class and spoke at his  high school graduation two years later  my parents get married now keep in mind  my dad is still undocumented delivering  pizzas and attending night school but  undocumented nonetheless in the midst of  all this my mom gets pregnant with me  fast-forward to the night before I was  born my mom starts having contractions  as my parents are timing these  contractions getting ready to you know  have a baby  they hear a knock at the door with no  idea who it could be maybe a neighbor or  a friend checking in they opened the  door it was two immigration officers  they'd been tipped off about my parents  give us your documentation without the  proper paperwork the officers are going  to detain them right then and there my  mom the feistiest latina you will ever  know wasn't having it true to form she's  like we're not doing this right now I'm  pregnant I'm about to give birth any  second you can't do this so they were  issued a court summons for a week later  in the meantime I'm born in court they  were told that they had 30 days to leave  or risk being deported and if they were  deported their odds of ever coming back  were slim to none so they left back to  Brazil my mom's American visa was still  renewable if she were to return to  school so she enlisted in classes and  came back to America with me meanwhile  my dad is still in Brazil determined as  ever to be reunited with his family with  no job prospects and after having been  turned down numerous times for an  American visa my dad decided to make the  journey again this time it was going to  be as fast as possible he had been  referred to a guy who for a very steep  fee would be able to get my dad past all  of the immigration checkpoints and into  the u.s. the plan was for my dad to  board a u.s. bound bus and he would be  made aware of when to get on and off the  bus he had no choice he gave the man all  the money he had and risked everything  the day comes my dad is on the bus while  in the way there was an unexpected  checkpoint they searched the bus and an  immigration officer asked my dad for his  documentation he was caught he was  arrested he was sent to jail for days he  obsessed over how to escape at one point  he actually asked one of the guards if I  run will you shoot me and the guard was  like yeah for sure he heard rumors of a  few inmates who had managed to escape  even scarier he had heard about inmates  who had attempted to escape but got  caught and were beaten within an inch of  their lives  one day they handcuffed my dad along  with all the other Brazilian inmates and  taken to the Brazilian consulate so that  they can be fingerprinted and ID  so that they'll eventually be sent back  to Brazil in the midst of all this  commotion my dad saw an opportunity  while being led off the bus they took  his handcuffs off he was outside in the  light of day and the gates were still  open and he knew this is it it's now or  never so he made a run for it the fence  was closing in and he went and faster  the prison alarm went off  he's just able to slip through and gain  a head start into the city years before  there had been an earthquake so he was  able to hide among the rubble of homes  and abandoned buildings near the prison  he could hear the police sirens as they  patrolled the area searching for him he  just kept running making his way from  spot to spot trying to get farther and  farther from all the chaos running until  he was far enough away that he could no  longer hear the police chatter the call  of the sirens with nowhere else to turn  he made his way to a place that could be  his last chance  the closest Mormon Chapel no one is  there eventually a janitor showed up and  my dad tells him about trying to make it  back to his wife and daughter in America  about the guy who was supposed to help  him avoid the immigration checkpoints on  the bus to the border about how he was  in jail and suddenly the janitor cuts in  wait what did you say what was that  guy's name turns out the janitor knew  the mother of the man who scammed my dad  as in the guy my dad gave all his money  to to avoid the checkpoints on the bus  apparently this woman attended the  church they were standing at so the  janitor took my dad's in her house they  get there she opened the door and my dad  asked her if she's the mother of  so-and-so she takes one look at my dad  sighs and replies what has he done to  you she was so kind my dad was able to  shower and II he even got to call my mom  and tell her that he was okay  for context my mom had no idea where my  dad was she hadn't heard from him since  he gotten arrested from the start she  didn't want him making this journey  again but at this point he was already  in too deep and so the church people  there put my dad in touch with the  church people in the following  neighborhood and he went on and on until  he was across the border from McAllen  Texas he'd been told out lots of  businessmen crossed the border at  McAllen every day all the businessmen  did was declare I'm an American citizen  and then they walked right in so the  church folks gave my dad a suit and a  briefcase for his belongings they  organized for an American citizen to  meet my dad on the other side my dad  walked past Border Patrol and declared  in the most bogus American accent I'm an  American citizen  it worked my dad met the American  citizen and they drove to the airport  my mom had purchased my dad an airline  ticket and she knew that if he could  just get onto that fight he'd be in the  clear the McAllen Airport being so close  to the border is filled with immigration  agents so my dad had been advised not to  stare at anyone or draw attention to  himself just be normal  he got his boarding pass and hit it to  his gate just mind your business and  read your newspaper he said to himself  he boarded the plane without a problem  made a transfer at San Antonio in  finally touchdown in Salt Lake City he  did it he made his way back to his  family  [Music]  my mom's entire family was at the  airport waiting for him including baby  me and then they lived happily ever  after in America I'm totally kidding it  would take many years of hard work  sacrifice and frankly sheer luck before  they'd be able to secure green cards but  they went on to raise a big family with  four kids and enjoy careers in tech and  finance and that's pretty remarkable  that a guy who just walked right into  the u.s. with less than $100 to his name  who attended high school in his 20s and  worked for years as an undocumented  immigrant paying taxes by the way made  it I have friends who can trace their  ancestry back to pioneers who crossed  the plains immigrants who entered Ellis  Island and yet the American Dream in my  family you  only a generation away I like to think  that there are a lot of stories like  this still happening today  [Music]
 

